# ScoreSense ETL & jobs pipeline

## Memory management

- Do not load multi-season play-by-play into memory at once.
- Prefer season-scoped reads, column pruning (`read_parquet(columns=[...])`), and chunked processing.
- Drop large intermediate DataFrames (`del df`) before the next join when processing nflverse data.

## Idempotency

- Refresh jobs (`weekly_refresh`, `preseason_refresh`) must be safe to re-run.
- Overwrite parquet/CSV artifacts in place — no duplicate rows on rerun.

## Atomic artifact writes

- Write to a `.tmp` path first, then `Path.replace()` to the final path.
- Prevents API reads of half-written pool or weekly prediction files.
- `save_pool_artifact` / `save_weekly_artifact` should follow this pattern when extended.

## Cache rebuild hooks

- After ETL + predict in refresh jobs, call `save_pool_artifact(season)` and `save_weekly_artifact(...)` as appropriate.
- Saving refreshes on-disk artifacts and in-process cache entries — see cache lifecycle in `draft-hub-performance.mdc`.

## External APIs

- Use existing integration modules (`src/integrations/`) with their cache/retry patterns.
- Do not add unbounded retry loops; respect rate limits for FantasyPros and similar APIs.

## Production refresh (VPS)

- Server path: `/root/scoresense`; run jobs inside container: `docker compose -f deploy/docker-compose.prod.yml exec -T api python -m src.jobs.preseason_refresh --draft-season 2026`
- Optional cron (Tuesdays 10:00 UTC): `docker compose -f deploy/docker-compose.prod.yml --profile cron run --rm refresh`
- After retrain/ETL on server: run `scripts/ops/fix_artifact_fingerprints.py` so cached weekly + draft pool artifacts are not rejected.
